    {
      "id": "s33",
      "component": "highlight",
      "props": {
        "title": "Exam Trap",
        "body": "One more exam note. 'Virtual representation' is Parliament's line, never the colonists'. If you hand it to the wrong side, the whole paragraph falls apart. And the trap here: don't write that the colonists told Parliament it had no power at all. In sixty-five they were denying one power, the power to tax them, while still calling themselves British subjects.",
        "highlights": [
          {
            "text": "Virtual representation is Parliament's line, never the colonists'"
          },
          {
            "text": "denying one power, the power to tax them"
