      "id": "s49",
      "component": "highlight",
      "props": {
        "title": "A1 Actual Representation",
        "body": "Actual representation. Taxation needs consent through a body you elected. Twenty-seven delegates from nine colonies drew it up in October sixty-five, right after the Stamp Act, and the logic is that Parliament's virtual representation line was invented to answer this very cry: a London MP who never faced colonial voters can't consent for a Boston printer. The consent has to come from our side.",
